---
import DiagramShell from "./DiagramShell.astro";
---

<DiagramShell
  title="Complete governed AI transaction"
  caption="BeaconGuard authorizes provider invocation and, separately, the declared enterprise action. AI output remains an untrusted proposal. BeaconGuard authorizes; the enterprise application executes."
  className="bg-diagram--governed-transaction"
>
  <div class="bg-txn" role="list">
    <div class="bg-flow-step bg-txn-app" role="listitem">Enterprise Application</div>
    <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>

    <div class="bg-flow-step bg-flow-step--boundary" role="listitem">
      Request Admission Authorization
    </div>

    <div class="bg-txn-fork" aria-label="Request admission outcomes">
      <div class="bg-txn-arm bg-txn-arm--deny">
        <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-deny">
          <strong>DENY</strong>
          <span>Record decision · No provider invocation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-txn-arm bg-txn-arm--allow">
        <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-allow">
          <strong>ALLOW</strong>
          <span>Provider invocation permitted</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-step bg-txn-provider" role="listitem">AI Provider</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-step bg-txn-result" role="listitem">
          AI-Generated Result
          <span>Untrusted proposal</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-step" role="listitem">
          Bind to Governed Transaction Context
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-step" role="listitem">
          Declare Intended Enterprise Action
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="bg-flow-step bg-flow-step--boundary" role="listitem">
          Result-to-Action Authorization
        </div>
        <div class="bg-txn-fork bg-txn-fork--nested" aria-label="Action authorization outcomes">
          <div class="bg-txn-arm bg-txn-arm--deny">
            <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-deny">
              <strong>DENY</strong>
              <span>Record decision · No enterprise effect</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-txn-arm bg-txn-arm--allow">
            <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-allow">
              <strong>ALLOW</strong>
              <span>Authorized action may proceed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
            <div class="bg-flow-step bg-txn-app" role="listitem">
              Enterprise Application Executes Authorized Action
            </div>
            <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
            <div class="bg-flow-step bg-txn-sor" role="listitem">
              Enterprise System of Record
              <span>Remains authoritative</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-evidence bg-txn-evidence" role="listitem">
      <strong>Decision evidence</strong>
      <span>Inspectable through BeaconGuard Verify</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div slot="text">
    <p>
      Enterprise Application → Request Admission Authorization. DENY records the
      decision and blocks provider invocation. ALLOW permits AI Provider
      invocation. The AI-Generated Result is an untrusted proposal. The
      enterprise application binds transaction context, declares the Intended
      Enterprise Action, and BeaconGuard evaluates Result-to-Action
      Authorization. DENY blocks enterprise effect. ALLOW lets the enterprise
      application execute the authorized action into the Enterprise System of
      Record. Authorization decisions produce evidence for BeaconGuard Verify.
    </p>
    <p>
      Result-to-Action Authorization means authorization of the declared
      intended enterprise action under the Active Verified Release. It does not
      mean semantic scoring of model content, and it does not resume or mutate
      a prior DENY.
    </p>
  </div>
</DiagramShell>
